/// The woody albedo model: a single parametric reflectance spectrum fitted to
/// bark, branches, stems, and sawn timber. The corpus is small (34 spectra
/// over 18 taxa) and the five parameters below are what that much data
/// honestly supports. Tabulated logit-space component curves are combined
/// linearly per wavelength with weights derived from five normalized [0, 1]
/// parameters, and the logistic link maps the result back to a reflectance, so
/// every output is strictly inside (0, 1) by construction. Every parameter is
/// saturated to [0, 1] at entry, by the fit warp.
///
/// Starting points for 13 familiar surfaces ship as the `WOODY_PRESET_*`
/// constants at the end of this module: barks named by their tree, the
/// chaparral by its community, the timber by its product. Each is a
/// 5-component vector in the parameter order below, to be expanded with
/// call-site `inline`.
///
/// Eleven of the thirteen are one real measured spectrum at its own fitted
/// coordinates, reconstructing that measurement within 4.90 dE. That bound is
/// not this model's accuracy but the material's own: two pieces of bark off
/// the same trunk disagree by 4.90 dE. Where taxa sit closer together than
/// that floor, as the dark conifer barks do, one preset stands for the group
/// at its medoid and says so.
///
/// The last two are marked `DERIVED`: a named preset with a single axis moved,
/// reaching where an air-dry, uniformly tinted corpus cannot.
/// `WEATHERED_GREY` is the sawn beam with `tannin` at 0, which is silvered
/// barn board; since the pigment curve is confined to the visible, it is the
/// measured timber unchanged across the whole SWIR. `RAIN_SOAKED` drives
/// `water`, whose curve is borrowed from the regolith model's wetting series,
/// past anything a bark corpus ever measured.
#smdl

using ::math import *;

// The logistic link, mapping a logit-space value back to (0, 1). The rails
// are float32 housekeeping, not a modeling choice: past |z| ~ 17 the true
// value would round to exactly 1.0, handing an infinity to any caller that
// takes -log(1 - R). The wood parameter box only reaches |z| ~ 9, so the
// rails are dormant here; they are kept so the strict (0, 1) guarantee is
// structural rather than an accident of the current tables.
@(pure macro)
auto link(const auto z) = #min(#max(1.0 / (1.0 + #exp(-z)), 1.0e-7), 0.9999999);

/// The minimum wavelength of the woody albedo table in nanometers.
export const float WOODY_MIN_WAVELENGTH = 400.0;
/// The maximum wavelength of the woody albedo table in nanometers.
export const float WOODY_MAX_WAVELENGTH = 2500.0;
/// The number of entries in the woody albedo table.
export const int WOODY_TABLE_SIZE = 124;

// smdl format off
